   "rule": {
    "type": "manual",
    "text": "Students may take 2 additional courses in BUDDSTD or from relevant courses in the departments of East Asian Languages and Cultures, South and Southeast Asian Studies, and History of Art. See an advisor for details.\nComplete at least 2 of:\n- Any BUDDSTD 100-196 level course\n- Any course related to Buddhist Studies in the subjects of CHINESE, EALANG, JAPAN, MONGOLN, SASIAN, SSEASN, or TIBETAN\n- HISTART 134A: Topics in Buddhist Art and Architecture: Buddhist Temple Art & Architecture in Japan\n- HISTART 134B: Topics in Buddhist Art and Architecture: Buddhist Icons in Japan … (see the catalog for the rest)",
    "mentionedCourses": [
     "HISTART 134A",
     "HISTART 134B",
